<title>MALAWI: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MALAWI GOVERNMENT LIST (970719)</p>
<p>*************************************************************</p>
<p>* 19 Jul 97 - The government announced it had dissolved its *</p>
<p>*		 cabinet in order to form a smaller one. It was*</p>
<p>*		 not known when President Muluzi would announce*</p>
<p>*		 the new cabinet.					*</p>
<p>*************************************************************</p>
<p> President.........Bakili MULUZI</p>
<p>Vice-President..Justin MALEWEZI</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Defence)</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING CABINET (Reshuffled 18 July 96):</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Livestock Development............Mapopa CHIPETA</p>
<p> Commerce &amp; Industry..........Chakakala CHAZIYA</p>
<p> Defence......See Vice-President</p>
<p>Education.....Donton MKANDAWIRE</p>
<p>Energy &amp; Mining....Dumbo LEMANI</p>
<p> Finance, Economic Planning &amp; Development..........Aleke BANDA</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs....George MTAFU</p>
<p> Forestry &amp; Natural Resources.......Melvyn MOYO</p>
<p> Health &amp; Population............Ziliro CHIBAMBO</p>
<p>Home Affairs....Robson MAKUWIRA</p>
<p> Housing......Kamangazi CHAMBALO</p>
<p>Information, Broadcasting, Posts &amp;</p>
<p>    Telecommunications........Brown MPINGANJIRA</p>
<p>Irrigation &amp; Water Development..Edward BWANALI</p>
<p> Justice Minister &amp; Attorney General..........Cassim CHILUMPHA</p>
<p>Labour &amp; Manpower Development.Kaliyoma PHUMISA</p>
<p>Lands &amp; Valuation...Peter FACHI</p>
<p> Local Government &amp; Rural Development...........Matembo NZUNDA</p>
<p> Physical Planning &amp; Surveys.......Edda CHITALO</p>
<p> Relief &amp; Rehabilitation......Richard SEMBEREKA</p>
<p> Research &amp; Environmental Affairs...........Mayinga MKANDAWIRE</p>
<p> State............Joseph KUBWALO</p>
<p> Tourism...........Patrick MBEWE</p>
<p> Transport &amp; Civil Aviation......Harry THOMPSON</p>
<p>Women, Children Affairs, Community</p>
<p>Development &amp; Social Welfare...Lilian PATEL</p>
<p>Works &amp; Supplies..Abdul PILLANE</p>
<p> Youth, Sports &amp; Culture........Bundaunda PHIRI</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor...........Matt CHIKAONDA</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			 (End Government List)</p>
